      "value": "@{68098a4626271974ef4d2775|full_name}\n\n//Edit 2\n\n1. Fewer uploads to VRChat storage = lower storage costs for VRChat.\n\n2. Less chaos in the user's \"Uploaded\" tab = more control and easier avatar management.\n\n3. Fewer draw calls, fewer materials, less skinning, fewer meshes, and less texture memory = better performance.\n\n4. Fewer PhysBone component allocations = less CPU overhead.\n\n5. Fewer duplicated avatar uploads = cleaner creator workflows.\n\n6. Less unused outfit data being loaded = lower memory usage in public instances.\n\n7. Better optimization without forcing creators to remove customization options.\n\nIt does not matter if the avatar still stays at Poor or Very Poor. There are several users, including myself, who have every avatar enabled regardless of rank.\n\nIf this optimization were implemented by VRChat developers, it would mean more free frames for me while I would still visually see no difference.\n\nIt is literally a free win for professionals and for avatar creator noobs.",
